.TH EPOLL_CTL 3crunch "" "Crunch" "Crunch Library Manual"
.SH NAME
epoll_ctl \- Linux x86-64 syscall 233
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <sys/syscall_220_259.h>
.B int epoll_ctl(int epoll, int operation, int descriptor, const void* event);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Controls an epoll instance. The event uses the packed 12-byte Linux x86-64 kernel layout.
This is a direct Linux x86-64 syscall wrapper; availability and permissions depend on the kernel and security policy.
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns the syscall result, or \-1 with errno set on failure.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR epoll_ctl (2)
